Third-party material
--------------------

The raft binary is built from Rust crates, each under its own licence. Their full
licence texts and copyright notices are in THIRD-PARTY.txt, next to this file.
That includes the fonts egui builds into the binary (crate epaint_default_fonts):

- Ubuntu Light, Ubuntu Font Licence 1.0
- Hack, MIT and the Bitstream Vera licence
- Noto Emoji, SIL Open Font License 1.1
- emoji-icon-font and egui-icons, MIT, Copyright (c) 2014 John Slegers

build-catalog and rename-books are Python scripts of Raft. At run time they call
programs that are not part of Raft and are not shipped with it: poppler-utils,
djvulibre, tesseract, Python 3 with Pillow and, optionally, the claude CLI.
